# 1. What is an Array?

An **Array** is a data structure used to store multiple elements in **contiguous memory locations**.

📌 Definition:

> An array is a **collection of elements stored in sequential memory**.

Example:

```python
arr = [10, 20, 30, 40]
```

Here:

| Index | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| 0     | 10    |
| 1     | 20    |
| 2     | 30    |
| 3     | 40    |

---

# 2. Array Characteristics

| Feature           | Explanation                        |
| ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Contiguous Memory | Elements stored next to each other |
| Indexed Access    | Access using index                 |
| Ordered           | Elements maintain order            |
| Fast Access       | O(1) lookup                        |

Example:

```python
arr[0]   # first element
arr[2]   # third element
```

---

# 3. Python vs Other Languages

| Language       | Array Behavior |
| -------------- | -------------- |
| C / C++ / Java | Fixed size     |
| Python         | Dynamic size   |

Example:

C++:

```cpp
int arr[5];
```

Python:

```python
arr = [1,2,3,4]
```

Python arrays can **grow dynamically**.

